==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|morn}}, from {{inh|en|ang|morgen}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*morgan}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*morgin}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*murganaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*murginaz}} (compare {{cog|fy|moarn}}, {{cog|nds|Morgen}}, {{cog|nl|morgen}}, {{cog|de|Morgen}}, {{cog|da|morgen}}, {{cog|no|morgon}}), from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*mr̥kéno}}, {{m|ine-pro|*mr̥kóno}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*mr̥Hko}} (compare <!--{{cog|cy|bore|t=morning}}, -->{{cog|lt|mérkti|t=to blink, twinkle}}, {{cog|sa|मरीचि|tr=márīci|t=ray of light}}), from {{m|ine-pro|*mer-|t=to shimmer, glisten}} (compare {{cog|el|μέρα|t=morning}}). {{doublet|en|morrow|morgen}}. See also {{m|en|morning}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/mɔːn/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/moɹn/|[mo̞ɹn]}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)n|s=1}}
* {{homophone|en|mourn|q1=with [[horse-hoarse merger]]|mourne|morne}}
* {{a|horse-hoarse}}<!--{{q|without the ''horse-hoarse'' merger}}--> 
** {{a|rhotic}} {{IPA|en|/mɔːɹn/}}
** {{a|nonrhotic}} {{IPA|en|/mɔːn/}}

